# core.autocrlf is true on this machine and git guesses binary-vs-text from the
# first 8000 bytes. assets/downloads/multiplication-mastery-pack.pdf contains no
# NUL byte anywhere, so git classified it as TEXT (`i/lf w/lf`, unlike every other
# binary here) and a fresh Windows clone would rewrite its line endings and check
# out a corrupt file — while every check on this machine kept passing, because the
# local copy was never converted. That PDF is the site's main free offer.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
